{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion","id":1442280,"title":"Garou religion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-01T10:32:59-07:00","id":1442280,"title":"Garou religion","content":"As I return to Werewolf: the Apocalypse after about a 20 year hiatus, it seems to me that the belief system outlined therein could easily be adopted as an actual real-world religion. It already comes complete with pagan deities and the bare bones of rituals and prayers. <br /> Has anyone heard of any person or group using as an actual religion? <br /> Understand that I mean this to be a fun discussion topic. I'm not actually trying to start a church or anything (well, unless anyone's interested. lol). I am fully aware that Werewolf is mythical symbolism, but in my view, so are all religions, so why not use it if it appeals to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T11:33:47-07:00","id":1442291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CultofJimmy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion#post1442280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I return to Werewolf: the Apocalypse after about a 20 year hiatus, it seems to me that the belief system outlined therein could easily be adopted as an actual real-world religion. It already comes complete with pagan deities and the bare bones of rituals and prayers.<br /> Has anyone heard of any person or group using as an actual religion?<br /> Understand that I mean this to be a fun discussion topic. I'm not actually trying to start a church or anything (well, unless anyone's interested. lol). I am fully aware that Werewolf is mythical symbolism, but in my view, so are all religions, so why not use it if it appeals to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it basically has a lot of this due to being a sort of &quot;interfaith smoothie&quot; of real life religions already. Sort of like the Force and Jedi.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T17:07:04-07:00","id":1442339,"title":"","content":"I don't see how you turn WtA animism into a functional real world faith. It relies too much on things that don't exist in the real world.<br /> <br /> It's also significantly different from Jediism. Beyond the practical matters (Star Wars is orders of magnitudes bigger as a fandom than WtA and only a tiny fraction of SW fans practice Jediism), Jediism fulfills a spiritual place that doesn't exist for a lot of modern people as a secular spiritual movement for people that want the positive aspects of organized religion without the dogma of traditional faiths. People interested in a constructed modern animist faith have options in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T19:06:56-07:00","id":1442346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442339#post1442339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how you turn WtA animism into a functional real world faith. It relies too much on things that don't exist in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, Environmentalist Pantheistic Animism would be pretty much identical anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T00:53:39-07:00","id":1442373,"title":"","content":"Given how much of Garou religion is based on their active interaction with spirits, I don't see how anything IRL could approach identical. Even Kinfolk are presented as not following the Garou religion even though some try to approximate it, because they have no real way to enact things their family members can. If Kinfolk in-setting for the most part can't connect to the religion because of their disconnect from the spirits, how is a real world practice going to get its practitioners to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T09:08:41-07:00","id":1442402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442373#post1442373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how much of Garou religion is based on their active interaction with spirits, I don't see how anything IRL could approach identical. Even Kinfolk are presented as not following the Garou religion even though some try to approximate it, because they have no real way to enact things their family members can. If Kinfolk in-setting for the most part can't connect to the religion because of their disconnect from the spirits, how is a real world practice going to get its practitioners to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, in the same way any other religion in the real world works. I don't know many Christians, Muslims or Wiccans who can claim to have seen their gods face to face or had supernatural encounters. Those who do claim such things, well, I'm pretty skeptical about that. <br /> I suppose the Garou religion in the real world would be a kind of amped up paganism, incorporating various pagan archetypes with a strong emphasis on environmentalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T13:54:50-07:00","id":1442434,"title":"","content":"But that's the exact problem. Real world religions are built on a foundation of indirect interaction with the divine/spiritual. You pray, you make sacrifices, you do rituals, and you send it out hoping it will be answers as you wish. Garou religion is built on the fact that they can literally summon up spiritual servants of their divine patrons whenever they want to directly ask them stuff, and travel to spiritual Realms to meet with the actual major spirits if they really want to.<br /> <br /> And we're largely skipping over the fact that the Garou religion is a warrior cult of fanatics, not some peaceful group of Earth-Mother worshipers.<br /> <br /> Since you can't do any of that in the real world, why would anyone want to be part of a religion that only makes sense if you can? Why not just become a Wiccan and then work on environmental issues? It's not like you're going to form packs, turn into supernatural monsters, and tear down fossil fuel companies before disappearing into the spirit world so that the authorities can't stop you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T22:38:11-07:00","id":1442461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442339#post1442339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also significantly different from Jediism. Beyond the practical matters (Star Wars is orders of magnitudes bigger as a fandom than WtA and only a tiny fraction of SW fans practice Jediism), Jediism fulfills a spiritual place that doesn't exist for a lot of modern people as a secular spiritual movement for people that want the positive aspects of organized religion without the dogma of traditional faiths. People interested in a constructed modern animist faith have options in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I think Heavy Arms is probably right that the correct answer to &quot;why don't we have a Garou-inspired religion yet?&quot; is &quot;there are not enough WtA fans to support the radical minority that would buy in to that extent.&quot; I am extremely disappointed by it, but it's probably the correct answer. I probably would not be surprised if there was at least one person on Earth for every World of Darkness gameline that does believe them to some case of &quot;The Truth&quot; being leaked, or something along those lines. But a few oddball cultists performing rituals privately is not a religion. That takes numbers.<br /> <br /> And I would like to take that last bit about &quot;options in the real world&quot; and expand on it, maybe even rant about it a wee bit. While the above answer is probably why there *isn't* one, I'd consider this a reason that there *shouldn't*. As noted above by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> , a lot of the reason that things like the mythology in WtA or Jedi philosophy in Star Wars seem to carry significant meaning or messages is because they have borrowed them from real existing philosophies and religions. To the extent that there is valuable truth to be found, it is more likely to be found in the source material that it was borrowed from, not the theme-park version put together for people to have fun rolling dice and messing around.<br /> <br /> Moreover, religions are generally based on the premise that they have knowledge of deeper metaphysical truths about reality. Unless you are suggesting that the writers of the World of Darkness were in fact some kind of esoteric conspiracy trying to spread a hidden spiritual message in the form of a game series, something that explicitly understands itself to be fiction seems like a poor source of religious guidance compared to the actual real-world religions and philosophies that were used to help inspire that fiction.<br /> <br /> To go back to Jediism for a moment, it mostly manages to avoid this problem by being, in practice, more of a philosophy or mindset that an adherence to any kind of metaphysical truth, especially given that there does not seem to be any kind of solid position on the only metaphysical component of the &quot;Jedi religion,&quot; the Force. And it can kind of get away with this because Star Wars itself (the movies at least) rarely went much into the deeper whys and hows of the Force. A &quot;Garou Religion&quot; is committed to a much stricter set of beliefs about particular entities and forces and the relationships between them than a nebulous &quot;energy&quot; connecting everything. Why would you choose to believe in the explicitly fictional Triat instead of a different set of pagan deities that many people have believed or currently believe in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T01:19:03-07:00","id":1442472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442434#post1442434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's the exact problem. Real world religions are built on a foundation of indirect interaction with the divine/spiritual. You pray, you make sacrifices, you do rituals, and you send it out hoping it will be answers as you wish. Garou religion is built on the fact that they can literally summon up spiritual servants of their divine patrons whenever they want to directly ask them stuff, and travel to spiritual Realms to meet with the actual major spirits if they really want to.<br /> <br /> And we're largely skipping over the fact that the Garou religion is a warrior cult of fanatics, not some peaceful group of Earth-Mother worshipers.<br /> <br /> Since you can't do any of that in the real world, why would anyone want to be part of a religion that only makes sense if you can? Why not just become a Wiccan and then work on environmental issues? It's not like you're going to form packs, turn into supernatural monsters, and tear down fossil fuel companies before disappearing into the spirit world so that the authorities can't stop you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think that's drawing a distinction that most Garou wouldn't really care about. As far as Garou are concerned, Kinfolk do follow the same religion. They're closer to the Spirits because they were blessed by Luna and Gaia but the whole making pacts and slaying Banes element isn't going to make a difference to their faithfulness.<br /> <br /> As for why people would want to follow a WTA religion. I imagine it's two things:<br /> <br /> 1. They believe the fundamentals are true. I.e. everything has a spirit and environment=good. Spiritual corruption=bad.<br /> <br /> 2. They're taking the piss to a certain level.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T04:35:43-07:00","id":1442481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442472#post1442472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I think that's drawing a distinction that most Garou wouldn't really care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have to. Real people trying to form a religion based on the Garou in the real world would though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. They believe the fundamentals are true. I.e. everything has a spirit and environment=good. Spiritual corruption=bad. </div> </div> </div>And this ignores a huge amount of what makes the Garou religion what it is to such a generic level that only people taking a piss would claim to follow it.<br /> <br /> The Garou religion isn't just &quot;environment = good,&quot; but, &quot;you have divine justification and duty to kill people that are an active threat to the environment.&quot; That isn't a fringe or radical part of the Garou religion, that's mainstream for them as they quibble about how bad &quot;active threat&quot; is. And in the real world there's no Pentex or BSDs to be bigger threats to say it's justified to ignore normal humans until you're done with the ones that actively and knowingly worship spiritual corruption.<br /> <br /> I know this is supposed to be mostly silly, but it's hard to keep it light if we're going to conflate real peaceful animist environmentalists with violent and murderous religious zealots by trying to ignore the parts that make the Garou fanatics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T04:39:49-07:00","id":1442483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442481#post1442481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't have to. Real people trying to form a religion based on the Garou in the real world would though.<br /> <br /> And this ignores a huge amount of what makes the Garou religion what it is to such a generic level that only people taking a piss would claim to follow it.<br /> <br /> The Garou religion isn't just &quot;environment = good,&quot; but, &quot;you have divine justification and duty to kill people that are an active threat to the environment.&quot; That isn't a fringe or radical part of the Garou religion, that's mainstream for them as they quibble about how bad &quot;active threat&quot; is. And in the real world there's no Pentex or BSDs to be bigger threats to say it's justified to ignore normal humans until you're done with the ones that actively and knowingly worship spiritual corruption.<br /> <br /> I know this is supposed to be mostly silly, but it's hard to keep it light if we're going to conflate real peaceful animist environmentalists with violent and murderous religious zealots by trying to ignore the parts that make the Garou fanatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I think that's seriously coming down on a very high cynicism interpretation of the Garou. Yes, they kill a lot of people and are religious fundamentalists but the people they primarily kill are a terrorist organization of demon-worshipers.<br /> <br /> Most Garou aren't randomly killing assholes off the street.<br /> <br /> I may be biased because I primarily play Children of Gaia, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T04:53:40-07:00","id":1442484,"title":"","content":"What exactly is cynical about it?<br /> <br /> In what modern country or society where people are theoretically considering adopting the Garou religion as their own is it acceptable for people to, &quot;kill a lot of people... but the people they <b>primarily</b> kill are a terrorist organization of demon-worshipers,&quot; based solely on faith-derived beliefs let lone a fringe modern creation?<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about random killing. I'm talking about specific targeted killing based on a set of values as taught by the Garou faith (which absolutely teaches you to kill certain types of people).<br /> <br /> Even the CoGs accept killing humans simply for being in the wrong place at the wrong time; even if they put more energy into avoiding that situation than the other Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T07:50:45-07:00","id":1442492,"title":"","content":"The OP can correct me if I am wrong, but I was assuming that the choice of name &quot;Garou Religion&quot; was less a reflection of a desire to mirror the Garou to such an extent that it included the militant radical holy war aspect, but rather a perhaps careless choice of words. My assumption has been that what they're really focused on is the spiritual and metaphysical aspects: the Triat, Gaia, Celestines, etc. &quot;Triat worship&quot; or the &quot;Gaian faith&quot; might have been better names. Obviously I made my feelings about that clear above. But perhaps give the OP the benefit of the doubt and not assume that they are advocating for environmental terrorism unless they explicitly signal it in some fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T09:40:29-07:00","id":1442500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442484#post1442484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is cynical about it?<br /> <br /> In what modern country or society where people are theoretically considering adopting the Garou religion as their own is it acceptable for people to, &quot;kill a lot of people... but the people they <b>primarily</b> kill are a terrorist organization of demon-worshipers,&quot; based solely on faith-derived beliefs let lone a fringe modern creation?<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about random killing. I'm talking about specific targeted killing based on a set of values as taught by the Garou faith (which absolutely teaches you to kill certain types of people).<br /> <br /> Even the CoGs accept killing humans simply for being in the wrong place at the wrong time; even if they put more energy into avoiding that situation than the other Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I feel like that's a very silly assumption to make about the adaptation of the books' characters to the setting.<br /> <br /> We could argue about RL ethics systems that also justify violence as well under certain circumstances. Particularly people who belong to various militaries and teach it as a form of self-defense or defense of others. It doesn't help that a lot of the Garou anger is driven by being tied to the struggle of RL Indigenous Peoples having their land stolen or destroyed.<br /> <br /> But that is beyond the scope of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T15:08:29-07:00","id":1442544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442492#post1442492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP can correct me if I am wrong, but I was assuming that the choice of name &quot;Garou Religion&quot; was less a reflection of a desire to mirror the Garou to such an extent that it included the militant radical holy war aspect, but rather a perhaps careless choice of words.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you can really separate those out as neatly as people are suggesting and be left with anything that really resembles the Garou in the end.<br /> <br /> It seems like what people want is more 1e Dreamspeakers (esp. the stuff that's easier for people to do without feeling appropriative of native and indigenous cultures), not Garou faith, in terms of a basis for a belief system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But perhaps give the OP the benefit of the doubt and not assume that they are advocating for environmental terrorism unless they explicitly signal it in some fashion. </div> </div> </div>Most of my stuff is actually a more strenuous response to CT's statement in post #4 than the OP's general idea. Though as I said, I'm not sure how you keep something Garou without the warrior part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442500#post1442500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I feel like that's a very silly assumption to make about the adaptation of the books' characters to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shifting from &quot;cynical&quot; to &quot;silly,&quot; doesn't clarify for me what you find objectionable about my characterization of the WtA setting and lore as presented in the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We could argue about RL ethics systems that also justify violence as well under certain circumstances. </div> </div> </div>I posed a specific question because it is specifically relevant to this topic. I think it avoids getting off-topic via wider scale ethical discussions fairly neatly.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm looking at how WtA presents the Garou and their faith, and the real world, and seeing a lot of reasons why people would not go, &quot;hey, I want to model my life around that!&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;kill for Gaia!&quot; thing is certainly a turn off to consider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't help that a lot of the Garou anger is driven by being tied to the struggle of RL Indigenous Peoples having their land stolen or destroyed. </div> </div> </div>Huh? Two Tribes focus on this out of 13. And, of course, RL native and indigenous peoples already have religions. They don't need a fictional one out of a gaming book, and if you care about their struggles, you probably don't want to seem like the kinda of unhelpful person that would adopt a similar faith designed in a fictional game by white people in some sort of performative attempt to demonstrate your allyship with them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T15:12:59-07:00","id":1442545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442544#post1442544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? Two Tribes focus on this out of 13. And, of course, RL native and indigenous peoples already have religions. They don't need a fictional one out of a gaming book, and if you care about their struggles, you probably don't want to seem like the kinda of unhelpful person that would adopt a similar faith designed in a fictional game by white people in some sort of performative attempt to demonstrate your allyship with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the Croatoan and Bunyip.<br /> <br /> Marginalized peoples also reflect other tribal struggles too.<br /> <br /> No, the fact is that there's a very good argument that Garou religion's violence reflects the struggle of people to take their land. Condemning it condemns the real life struggle and I'm not comfortable doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T15:54:59-07:00","id":1442548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442545#post1442545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the Croatoan and Bunyip.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're dead. They're not a primary source of Garou anger when they're not alive to be angry. Those angry about the Croatoan are the two Tribes I mentioned, and no Garou in general are angry about the Bunyip as opposed to shamed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Marginalized peoples also reflect other tribal struggles too. </div> </div> </div>O...K... I really have no idea what you're going on about with this statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, the fact is that there's a very good argument that Garou religion's violence reflects the struggle of people to take their land. </div> </div> </div>Even more confused who exactly you're talking about; esp. with the topic of the thread being about adopting Garou religion IRL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Condemning it condemns the real life struggle and I'm not comfortable doing so. </div> </div> </div>Where did this even come from?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T16:48:08-07:00","id":1442558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442548#post1442548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did this even come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've done a blanket condemnation of violence in the religion when I pointed out that violence is a major part of many cultures the Garou reference in resisting oppression. So it's weird that you bring it up.<br /> <br /> But yes, I get it. You think it's a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T17:19:07-07:00","id":1442562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442558#post1442558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've done a blanket condemnation of violence in the religion when I pointed out that violence is a major part of many cultures the Garou reference in resisting oppression.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't make any blanket condemnation. I posed a question (which you never answered) about the acceptance of religiously motivated violence in general society by the real people that would be considering creating/joining a Garou based religion IRL.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;rebuttal&quot; has gotten so ridiculous that I'm not sure if you're joking, or if you're seriously trying to argue some of the things you're saying because they come off as really ugly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it's weird that you bring it up. </div> </div> </div>How is it weird, when talking about the subject of the thread, to bring up the fact that the Garou religion is the religion of a violent fanatical cult that regularly enacts terrorist violence in the name of their faith?<br /> <br /> Is it really strange that a lot people that have ready WtA are going to go, &quot;Yeah, nobody IRL should try to follow this belief system because it's a radical violent ideology,&quot; to you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, I get it. You think it's a bad idea. </div> </div> </div>No, you don't seem to get it at all. I'm really not sure how to be more clear here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T19:51:09-07:00","id":1442574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442544#post1442544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure you can really separate those out as neatly as people are suggesting and be left with anything that really resembles the Garou in the end.<br /> <br /> It seems like what people want is more 1e Dreamspeakers (esp. the stuff that's easier for people to do without feeling appropriative of native and indigenous cultures), not Garou faith, in terms of a basis for a belief system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Most of my stuff is actually a more strenuous response to CT's statement in post #4 than the OP's general idea. Though as I said, I'm not sure how you keep something Garou without the warrior part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for misunderstanding and misrepresenting your point regarding militancy and violence.<br /> <br /> I actually agree with what you're saying here very much. That was what I was trying to get across with the point about &quot;Gaian Faith&quot; or something like that being a better term; the OP's choice of the word Garou was, presumably, a mistake of sorts. I think their point is about a religion based on the Triat, Gaia, the Umbra, etc. Not a point about being chosen spiritual warriors in a violent conflict with modern industrial polluters. I think this is also why comparisons to Kinfolk were made above, them being comparatively &quot;regular&quot; people that sometimes know about these spiritual matters and might share some of the broad metaphysical and ideological tenets of their Garou relatives; but it does fall short when you consider the specific relation that Kinfolk have with the chosen warriors of the Earth, the position of Garou dogma. I'm not especially familiar with the Dreamspeakers beyond the basics; you're probably right about it being a better analogy for the OP's position, but they might not be familiar enough with Mage to reference it from that perspective.<br /> <br /> Of course, if I am mistaken, and the OP is focused more on the Garou specifically as a model, it does raise questions about things like their position regarding violence, the elitism involved in viewing oneself as part of a group of &quot;chosen ones,&quot; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T23:46:58-07:00","id":1442588,"title":"","content":"The Dreamspeakers in 1e Mage were basically Gaian mages where the WtA cosmology was used as a &quot;universal&quot; animist/shaman religion/philosophy similar to how the Celestial Chorus has a universal monotheist religion that worships The One instead of actually continuing to strictly follow the religions many of their members had before joining the Chorus. Though Dreamspeakers as Gaian devotees was dropped fairly quickly in Mage because shoving every real world animist faith based mage into one Tradition, and then saying they all abandoned their people's faiths (many of which are dying out) to join one big generic one was a pretty boneheaded move and the Dreamspeakers were rewritten to be an alliance of all those different practices trying to survive all the things strangling those faiths ability to continue on.<br /> <br /> Besides not having the militancy of the Garou, the 1e Dreamspeakers had other differences: they didn't specifically venerate Luna or care that much about the Triat as specific entities in their own right. As well they didn't engage with the major Incarnae the same way, as they didn't have Totems (at least not in the sense WtA uses the term). But all that is a far more functional basis for RL people trying to create a WtA Gaian inspired faith rather than relying on the Garou's militant bend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T13:49:03-07:00","id":1442635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442492#post1442492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP can correct me if I am wrong, but I was assuming that the choice of name &quot;Garou Religion&quot; was less a reflection of a desire to mirror the Garou to such an extent that it included the militant radical holy war aspect, but rather a perhaps careless choice of words. My assumption has been that what they're really focused on is the spiritual and metaphysical aspects: the Triat, Gaia, Celestines, etc. &quot;Triat worship&quot; or the &quot;Gaian faith&quot; might have been better names. Obviously I made my feelings about that clear above. But perhaps give the OP the benefit of the doubt and not assume that they are advocating for environmental terrorism unless they explicitly signal it in some fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is correct. I was envisioning the use of the deities and spirits, as well as the cosmology as a guide. I would not think that people following such a philosophy would be compelled to believe that werewolves, fomori, etc. actually literally exist. <br /> Consider Dudeism, a religion based on The Big Lebowski. They find the Dude to be an inspirational figure and take lessons from the movie. Clearly they know that it's a work of fiction. <br /> Or hell, I even know Christians who don't believe that the Bible is literally true, or at least not all of it. To them, it doesn't much matter what theological beliefs you hold about Christ. It's about following the message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T13:58:10-07:00","id":1442636,"title":"","content":"I suppose a better phrasing would be &quot;a religion inspired by WtA,&quot; and not the actual Garou faith. One would have be delusional to believe they can actually sprout fur and claws and go fight Wyrm creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T14:45:38-07:00","id":1442642,"title":"","content":"I think the question still remains: what would actually draw people in then? The general WtA cosmology is interesting, but what lessons does it impart ala the Dude or Jesus or Buddha, or etc. that people would want to live by? Are any of those really unique enough to WtA that people wouldn't have already found those lessons in existing real world faith options?<br /> <br /> Because, to me at least, the WtA cosmology doesn't really have a message to follow. It's just a state of a fictional world that can be interpreted through many lenses (the Garou, the other Fera, 1e Dreamspeakers, etc.) which are what create the actual life lessons that might draw people in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T18:19:28-07:00","id":1442667,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms, I think people would be drawn to it if WtA resonates with them on a deep level. I'm guessing that's what motivates people to claim Jedi as their religion, even though Jedi beliefs are more or less a fictional version of Taoism. I suppose the parallel for Werewolf would be a deep dive into the pagan traditions that Werewolf draws from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T18:55:53-07:00","id":1442670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CultofJimmy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion#post1442280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I return to Werewolf: the Apocalypse after about a 20 year hiatus, it seems to me that the belief system outlined therein could easily be adopted as an actual real-world religion. It already comes complete with pagan deities and the bare bones of rituals and prayers. <br /> Has anyone heard of any person or group using as an actual religion? <br /> Understand that I mean this to be a fun discussion topic. I'm not actually trying to start a church or anything (well, unless anyone's interested. lol). I am fully aware that Werewolf is mythical symbolism, but in my view, so are all religions, so why not use it if it appeals to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but my college had a Gothic poetry night and someone I game with got up and read a poem from W20 (I think it was the When Will You Rage? poem). People loved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T19:20:17-07:00","id":1442672,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between &quot;this is cool because it resonates with me,&quot; and &quot;I want to live my life according to these teachings because this resonates with me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Jedi and even the Dude are offering something to people, even if they're just modern secularist remixes of existing philosophies. They speak to people beyond being cool because they offer a distillation of long standing and well developed teachings that are easily accessible for people that don't have simple access to traditional forms of them.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to point out, is that WtA doesn't have that sort of &quot;bridge,&quot; to be more appealing than existing real world modern animist faiths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T20:10:03-07:00","id":1442680,"title":"","content":"Even as one of the few people who love the Triat and the Umbra in general (basically everything related to Wraith/Ghosts and Spirits) and defends it constantly, people centering a whole religion around the stuff in WtA wouldn't make much sense. The fundamental aspect that sets apart what the Garou adhere to in WoD is that everything spirit related or in general ephemeral isn't based on faith, its something they interact with and directly commune with on a daily basis.<br /> <br /> They go into the Spirit Wilds for self-insight; they fight Banes as a continual religious sanctification in the name of Gaia; their oral recountings and maybe the odd written record here or there can be backed and decidedly proven (most of the time); the anathema to their adherence (the Wyrm and sometimes Weaver which I think is more deadly for the Garou in the long run) actually is active in corrupting the world, etc. One of the key fundamental parts of religion is &quot;faith&quot;, i.e trusting or believing without significant evidence. However as we know, the Triat &amp; generally Gaia doesn't have this aspect/component, because in WoD (and IN only WoD of course since it's a fictional universe), everything that transpires with it is &quot;real&quot;... so I don't know how it really classifies as religion as we know it IRL (not the say it isn't a religion or form of it, but not in our IRL context I mean).<br /> <br /> Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> says, there'd be no point for you to adhere to this religion from a Tabletop game since there is nothing you can glean from or have a real feeling toward it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T21:39:29-07:00","id":1442686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CultofJimmy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442635#post1442635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider Dudeism, a religion based on The Big Lebowski. They find the Dude to be an inspirational figure and take lessons from the movie. Clearly they know that it's a work of fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Red Talons are clearly correct, we all deserve to die for being part of a world where this has been allowed to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CultofJimmy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442635#post1442635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or hell, I even know Christians who don't believe that the Bible is literally true, or at least not all of it. To them, it doesn't much matter what theological beliefs you hold about Christ. It's about following the message.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad marks for me, not realizing that I was making assumptions about the presumed meaning of the word &quot;religion.&quot; Should've remembered the golden rule of definitions.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you want to call that &quot;religion,&quot; then yeah, believe in whatever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T21:57:48-07:00","id":1442688,"title":"","content":"Is there a sourcebook that goes into detail on Garou Religion, In particular I want yto know what's the official name or the religion, I imagine somethibg like &quot;the cult of Gaia&quot; or &quot;the gaian cult&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T03:01:30-07:00","id":1442697,"title":"","content":"The Revised Players Guide probably went into the most detail on Garou spirituality, but there's lots more scattered around the books and none go into exhaustive detail about it.<br /> <br /> The Garou don't have an official name for it because they don't actively perceive as a religion/faith/etc. in human terms. As has been noted, their belief structure is based on things that they actively perceive (though it does border on faith even if they don't acknowledge it when it comes to their ability to perceive the intentions of higher powered spirits as an example) and interact with. Most Garou would say it's more analogous to the pride felt when doing service to a greater good; such as obvious examples of patriotic pride in military service, and less overt examples like volunteering at a food bank.<br /> <br /> You could also say it relates to a strong tendency in early human groups (whether they only exist in historical record or have survived to modern times) to have names that translate to either &quot;humans&quot; or &quot;people&quot; and likewise don't have specific names for their religions/faiths/etc. They don't need names for themselves or what they belief, that's just normal, they have names for other people and other beliefs because those are different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T05:35:35-07:00","id":1442707,"title":"","content":"I just figured it wouldn't be too far out of place among the countless post-modern religions that have arisen in the last few decades, many of them based on something in pop culture. I can't really say how it would work in the real world, because it is only the seed of a thought that I threw out for an amusing discussion. I do not actually adhere to such a religion myself. If anything, I've found the myths presented in WtA to be an intro to researching the actual myths and traditions that inspired them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T08:41:19-07:00","id":1442727,"title":"","content":"Something I found myself pondering while considering one of my previous responses: the Litany. Would that qualify as part of a &quot;Garou Religion&quot;?<br /> <br /> Is the Litany an example of secular law or religious law, or is it one of those distinctions that just breaks down when applied to examples like the Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T09:02:49-07:00","id":1442729,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the idea of religion being based in believing in something you can't perceive is something of a very Western Post-Christianity thing. There's plenty of religions that believed in God Kings and non-theistic cultural laws.<br /> <br /> Hell, you talk to a sun worshiper 5000 years ago and he'd be like, &quot;What the fuck are you on about? It's right there.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442688#post1442688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a sourcebook that goes into detail on Garou Religion, In particular I want yto know what's the official name or the religion, I imagine somethibg like &quot;the cult of Gaia&quot; or &quot;the gaian cult&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it would be &quot;The Garou Nation&quot; since the entirety of the Garou race and sect is a cult as well as national as well as racial identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-05-2021, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T10:21:52-07:00","id":1442743,"title":"","content":"<b>How would Garouism work in the Real World?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, I've given it a name.<br /> <br /> If there was a &quot;semi-serious religious identity&quot; I would assume that the religious practitioners of Garouism would adopt the totem identity of being defenders of the Earth and Warriors for Gaia. You would adopt the mental identity of being a werewolf (even though you can't change form in RL) and fight against what you perceive to be mental and spiritual corruption in the real world. You are a &quot;warrior for Gaia&quot; even though said method of war would be with activism and focus rather than violence -- if for no other reason than you don't have superpowers and are not facing supernatural evils.<br /> <br /> Garousim would presumably be a pantheist religion which is neither non-theistic or theistic really as nature worship is something that doesn't actually require a matter of faith. Venerating the sun, ecosystem, and humanity's relationship with nature is something that many people do with &quot;spirits&quot; not necessarily being immortal or eternal but simply a part of the greater shared interlocking nature of the world.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/UsefulNotes/Pantheism\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...otes/Pantheism</a><br /> <br /> Using the metaphors of the Triat, a practitioner of Garouism would presumably attempt to be someone who would find balance in their own lives between being properly angry at injustices as well as systemic failures of humanity (Rage against the Wyrm) while also not losing control over these qualities. They would attempt to preserve a balance between the Wyld (Change) and Weaver (Stasis) while also recognizing that destruction or corruption has gone off course in human society (The Wyrm). Gaia doesn't require one to actually have a personal relationship with her because Gaia is the world and nature around us so we don't require faith as a matter of belief in this world.<br /> <br /> As stated the above is a pantheistic non-supernatural religion and non-supernatural religions DO exist but would be primarily viewed in the terms of a <b>life philosophy</b>. Garouism as something metaphorical and a tool for living your best life as well as working toward the preservation of the eco-system and spiritual unity with it that humanity has largely ignored.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernatural Garouism</b><br /> <br /> However, if you believe in it you could apply this to an animistic ancestor worshiping reincarnation based religion too. But you should probably not do that with an RPG as your basis, just an introduction to investigating whatever religions (Shinto, Hinduism, Buddism) that have that as actual belief structures.<br /> <br /> Because otherwise, that would be silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T14:13:57-07:00","id":1442767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CultofJimmy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442707#post1442707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I've found the myths presented in WtA to be an intro to researching the actual myths and traditions that inspired them.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not as big of a factor as some of the others brought up, I'd say this is a tertiary one that helps explain the lack of interest in this idea. While I see it more in Mage fans than WtA fans, WoD fans in general do tend to get into research of this sort. So the very fans most likely to develop an interest in an alternative spiritual lifestyle after reading the game the same ones most likely to learn about all the ones already out there instead of trying to create something from the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442729#post1442729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the idea of religion being based in believing in something you can't perceive is something of a very Western Post-Christianity thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the threadis addressing the idea of starting a new religion that is largely going to target people living in Western post-Christianity cultures as potential members?<br /> <br /> Though you seem to more importantly being skipping over the distinguishing factor of direct vs. indirect interactions with objects of spiritual importance. A sun worshiper from 5,000 years ago might be able to point to the sun and say, &quot;look it's right there,&quot; but they're can't show that anything they're doing is direct interaction with the sun. Garou can go talk to Helios if they want to spend the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T14:44:21-07:00","id":1442769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442743#post1442743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Garouism work in the Real World?<br /> <br /> Yes, I've given it a name.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's gonna sound like a furry cult in French speaking lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T15:15:46-07:00","id":1442772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Garou Nation&quot; since the entirety of the Garou race and sect is a cult as well as national as well as racial identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't know about that since there are other Changing Breeds/Fera that also revere Gaia and recognize the facets of the Triat aswell. &quot;Garou Nation&quot; or &quot;Garouism&quot; wouldn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T15:18:22-07:00","id":1442773,"title":"","content":"Garou Nation is in response to &quot;what would the Garou call their religion&quot; which is to say, they wouldn't see a separation between their religion and their society.<br /> <br /> Garouism only works if you're making a religion based on the game and decide to keep the Garou central and exclude the other Fera as part of the philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T16:07:19-07:00","id":1442778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442772#post1442772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I don't know about that since there are other Changing Breeds/Fera that also revere Gaia and recognize the facets of the Triat aswell. &quot;Garou Nation&quot; or &quot;Garouism&quot; wouldn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but their religion is objectively different in every case. They may revere the same gods but their interpretations are greatly different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442280-garou-religion?p=1442773#post1442773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou Nation is in response to &quot;what would the Garou call their religion&quot; which is to say, they wouldn't see a separation between their religion and their society.<br /> <br /> Garouism only works if you're making a religion based on the game and decide to keep the Garou central and exclude the other Fera as part of the philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I imagine so since the game is called Werewolf: The Apocalypse. Gaianism wouldn't work because there's already religions like that in RL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=s